            <node id="n2::n5::n4">
              <data key="d100">Sterol regulatory element-binding protein 2</data>
              <data key="d101">Class D basic helix-loop-helix protein 2; Sterol regulatory element-binding transcription factor 2</data>
              <data key="d104">Precursor of the transcription factor form (Processed sterol regulatory element-binding protein 2), which is embedded in the endoplasmic reticulum membrane. Low sterol concentrations promote processing of this form, releasing the transcription factor form that translocates into the nucleus and activates transcription of genes involved in cholesterol biosynthesis</data>
